            <ArticleTitle>Paraspinal abscess following facet joint injection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>52-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Injection to the zygapophysial joint is a procedure which is performed frequently for diagnostic or therapeutic reasons in the management of back pain. It is generally considered to be free of significant complications. We report a patient who developed a paraspinal abscess following a lumbar facet joint injection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
